{"step_index":248,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-06T13:31:30Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-06T15:31:30+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-06T15:31:31+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/qualification-verification-system/src/main/resources/templates/dashboard.html`\nTotal Lines: 478\nTotal Bytes: 26345\nShowing lines 415 to 478\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n415:         function showIssueForm() {\n416:             switchTab('qualificationsTab', document.getElementById('tabBtnQuals'));\n417:             const reg = document.getElementById('registerSection');\n418:             if (reg) reg.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth' });\n419:         }\n420: \n421:         document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {\n422:             // 1. Enforce authentication on dashboard\n423:             const token = getAuthToken();\n424:             if (!token) {\n425:                 window.location.href = '/login?notice=verify_required';\n426:                 return;\n427:             }\n428: \n429:             const user = getStoredUser();\n430: \n431:             // 2. Role-based adjustments\n432:             if (user && user.role === 'ROLE_VERIFIER') {\n433:                 const btnIssue = document.getElementById('btnIssueQual');\n434:                 if (btnIssue) btnIssue.style.display = 'none';\n435: \n436:                 const regSection = document.getElementById('registerSection');\n437:                 if (regSection) regSection.style.display = 'none';\n438: \n439:                 const title = document.getElementById('dashHeaderTitle');\n440:                 if (title) title.innerText = 'Accredited Credential Verification Portal';\n441: \n442:                 const sub = document.getElementById('dashHeaderSubtitle');\n443:                 if (sub) sub.innerText = 'Verify academic credentials, inspect blockchain blocks, and evaluate AI fraud heuristics.';\n444:             }\n445: \n446:             // 3. Tab routing via URL query parameter\n447:             const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);\n448:             const targetTab = params.get('tab');\n449:             const certQuery = params.get('cert');\n450: \n451:             if (targetTab === 'qualificationsTab') {\n452:                 switchTab('qualificationsTab', document.getElementById('tabBtnQuals'));\n453:             } else if (targetTab === 'blockchainTab') {\n454:                 switchTab('blockchainTab', document.getElementById('tabBtnBlockchain'));\n455:             } else if (targetTab === 'aiTab') {\n456:                 switchTab('aiTab', document.getElementById('tabBtnAi'));\n457:             } else if (targetTab === 'telemetryTab') {\n458:                 switchTab('telemetryTab', document.getElementById('tabBtnTelemetry'));\n459:             } else {\n460:                 // Default to Verification Console for authenticated users\n461:                 switchTab('verifyTab', document.getElementById('tabBtnVerify'));\n462:             }\n463: \n464:             // 4. Auto-verify if cert query parameter is present\n465:             if (certQuery) {\n466:                 const input = document.getElementById('verificationInput');\n467:                 if (input) input.value = certQuery;\n468:                 verifyCredential(certQuery);\n469:             }\n470: \n471:             // 5. Load data\n472:             loadQualifications();\n473:             fetchTelemetry();\n474:         });\n475:     </script>\n476: </body>\n477: </html>\n478: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":249,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-06T13:31:31Z","thinking":"**Implementing Role-Based Dashboard Display**\n\nAdding a role scope banner above the dashboard tabs is the first step. Next, the focus shifts to `DOMContentLoaded` to precisely configure tab visibility and the role scope display based on the user's role. Specifically, the display of specific dashboard elements like the qualifications tab, telemetry tab, and the issue qualifications button will be hidden based on the `ROLE_VERIFIER`. The role scope banner for `ROLE_VERIFIER` will be configured to show a magnifying glass icon and specific title.\n\n\n**Differentiating Role-Specific UI Elements**\n\nObserving that `ROLE_INSTITUTION` users (Officers) require specific UI elements, the next step involves making the necessary modifications to reveal and hide them based on the active role. Additionally, the telemetry tab will be hidden. Also, the revocation function will be disabled within the Officer's qualifications table.\n\nThe `ROLE_ADMIN` user requires complete system access.  All tabs and actions must be made available. This includes the exclusive revocation power.\n\nDocumenting role-specific access controls is crucial. The appropriate roleScopeBanner needs to be shown, using the provided data, which contains the icon, title, subtitle, and associated tags.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Add role scope banner and tab access controls to dashboard.html","EndLine":68,"Instruction":"Add roleScopeBanner in dashboard.html above dash-tabs","ReplacementContent":"            <button id=\"btnIssueQual\" class=\"btn-primary\" onclick=\"showIssueForm()\">\n                + Issue New Qualification\n            </button>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Role Permission Scope Banner -->\n        <div id=\"roleScopeBanner\" style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: cen